    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0059" n="51" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg51"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.00/921: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Batavia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dickover</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Batavia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-17T17:00:00+07:30">July 17, 1940—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 17—10:38 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have discussed the fall of the Cabinet<anchor n="90" xml:id="d68-f1"/> and the
                    rise of a presumably fascist party in Japan with several government officials
                    including the Governor General and the Admiral. They all are decidedly
                    apprehensive of future developments in the Far East, [as] Germany, Japan may be
                    preparing to seize this “golden opportunity” to eliminate Western influence and
                    to establish its “new order” in this part of the world. They all desired to know
                    what the United States would do in <pb facs="0060" n="52" xml:id="pg52"/> such
                    case, to which I replied that it depends on the will of the people as expressed
                    through Congress. I received the impression that the Netherlands Indies in this
                    period of crisis is more and more hoping for some indication that it will be
                    protected by the American fleet.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dickover</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d68-f1" n="90" xml:id="d68-f1-content">
                <p>For resignation of Admiral Yonai’s Cabinet on July 16, see telegram No. 590, July
                    17, 5 p.m., from the Ambassador in Japan, <ref target="#pg964">p. 964</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
